The '''2026–27 Süper Lig''', officially '''Trendyol Süper Lig Adnan Süvari season''', is the 69th season of the [[Süper Lig]], the highest tier [[Association football|football]] league of [[Turkey]]. It began on 14 August 2026. The season is set to end on 23 May 2027.<ref>{{cite web|access-date=24 March 2026 |date=6 March 2026 |language=tr |publisher=[[Turkish Football Federation]] |title=Profesyonel Liglerde 2026-2027 Sezonu Başlangıç Tarihleri Belli Oldu |url=https://www.tff.org/default.aspx?pageID=204&ftxtID=49875}}<!-- auto-translated from Turkish by Module:CS1 translator --></ref>

The season named after the former player and coach [[Adnan Süvari]], best known for his career in Göztepe, who died in 1991.

== Teams ==
Eighteen teams will compete in the league – the top fifteen teams from the [[2025–26 Süper Lig|previous season]] and the three teams promoted from the [[2025–26 TFF First League|First League]].

===Changes from last season===

==== Relegations ====
[[Antalyaspor]], [[Kayserispor]] and [[Fatih Karagümrük S.K.|Fatih Karagümrük]] were relegated to the [[2026–27 TFF 1. Lig]].

==== Promotions ====
[[Erzurumspor F.K.|Erzurumspor]] was promoted to Süper Lig after 5 seasons of absence. [[Amed S.F.K.]] and [[Çorum F.K.]] were promoted to Süper Lig for their first time in their histories.

